      <h3>Cold Start & Cooldown Analysis</h3>
      <p>The 2kW Incoloy heater draws from the LiFePO4 battery pack on cold start. At 2kW load, 15 gallons of water from ambient 20°C requires approximately 18–25 minutes to reach 90 PSI operating pressure, depending on ambient temperature and insulation efficiency.</p>
      <p>A pre-heated boiler (stored in a garage above 15°C) reaches operating pressure in 4–6 minutes — generator begins charging battery pack immediately once the engine turns over at minimum steam pressure (~60 PSI).</p>
      <p>Engine self-sustains: generator output at 200 RPM → ~1,200W. Boiler maintenance load ~800W. Net surplus to battery: ~400W at idle. Full surplus at operating speed.</p>
