      <h3>Start & Stop Procedure</h3>
      <p>1. Battery powers 2kW boiler heater. 18–25 minutes cold, 4–6 minutes pre-warmed.</p>
      <p>2. At 60 PSI minimum, crack steam to Piston A slowly. Engine begins to turn.</p>
      <p>3. Generator engages at ~50 RPM minimum. Battery begins receiving charge.</p>
      <p>4. Increase steam to operating pressure 110–130 PSI. Engine reaches 200–400 RPM.</p>
      <p>5. At operating RPM, system is fully self-sustaining. Battery surplus confirmed above 200 RPM.</p>
      <p>Stop: close PCW valves, engine decelerates, boiler retains pressure. Cool-down 35–50 min.</p>
    </div>
